winex11.drv: Apply constant layered alpha in the window surface.

Use the ARGB visual for local, non-embedded LWA_ALPHA windows below
full opacity when no colour key is requested and XRender is available:
without it the frames of 3D child windows cannot be copied into a 32-bit
window. Premultiply a separate upload image, preserving the GDI backing
pixels across repeated flushes.
Reuse win32u's existing alpha_bits and full-surface invalidation when
constant alpha changes. Do not change the driver interface.

Delete _NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY on this path, including window recreation,
so compositors honouring the hint do not apply the alpha a second time.
Keep the existing opacity-hint fallback without ARGB or XRender, or for
embedded and foreign windows. Full opacity, attribute removal and colour-key
requests retain the default-visual path; UpdateLayeredWindow is unchanged.

A window that shows its own OpenGL, Vulkan or Direct3D frames keeps the
default visual and the hint as well: the frames cover the surface and carry
no alpha. The window's state is updated when such frames come or go.

Applies to: Valve Wine fda79a5 (GE-Proton11-12) after GE's preparation, in order after 0007.
The driver interface version is unchanged (111).

